<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Default channel strip configuration for the CSurf Klinke MCU extension.

  This file is a READ-ONLY TEMPLATE. The deployment scripts copy it next to
  the plugin binary (e.g. ~/.config/REAPER/UserPlugins/) on every deploy.

  On first run (when no user file exists yet) the extension copies it to
  the user file:
      ~/.config/REAPER/MCU/ChannelStripMaps/channelstrips.xml   (Linux)
      <Documents>\Reaper\MCU\ChannelStripMaps\channelstrips.xml (Windows)
      ~/Library/Application Support/REAPER/MCU/ChannelStripMaps/channelstrips.xml (macOS)

  All user changes are written to the USER file only — this template is
  never modified by the extension, so redeploying can never clobber user
  data. The "Restore defaults" button in the channel strip editor copies
  this template back over the user file.

  Format: one <STRIP> per assigned slot (nr = 1..16) with its <VPOT>
  children. See src/modes/channelstrip/ChannelStripMap.h for the schema.
  The file is currently EMPTY — paste the <STRIP> elements of your
  preferred channelstrips.xml into the <CHANNELSTRIPS> root below.
-->
<CHANNELSTRIPS/>
